'''House Vizsla''' was one of the ruling [[Mandalorian house|houses]], or [[Politics|political]] factions, that made up [[Mandalorian]] society. It was headed by [[Clan Vizsla]]. Two of the [[Mandalorian clan|clans]] that allied with House Vizsla were [[Clan Wren]] and [[Clan Saxon]]. House Vizsla would be at the center of various conflicts in Mandalorian history, including the unification of [[Mandalore]] after [[Tarre Vizsla]]'s [[death]], a [[Mandalorian Civil War (19 BBY)|civil war]] during the [[Clone Wars]], and another [[Mandalorian Civil War (Imperial Era)|civil war]] during the [[Imperial Era]].

==Description==
House Vizsla was a [[Mandalorian house]], or [[Politics|political faction]] that was part of [[Mandalorian]] society and was led by [[Clan Vizsla]].<ref name="Protector Recon" /> House Vizsla also contained other [[Mandalorian clan]]s such as [[Clan Saxon]]<ref name="Zero Hour">{{Rebels|Zero Hour}}</ref> and [[Clan Wren]].<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|clan-wren|Clan Wren}}</ref> One member of House Vizsla, [[Tarre Vizsla]], created the [[Darksaber]], which became an important symbol of the house and respected by all others.<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" />

The house's emblem was a [[shriek-hawk]], a [[Diet|predatory]] [[bird]] native to Mandalore. It would also eventually become the emblem of the [[Death Watch]].<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> The house had a peacetime [[signet]] which predated the [[Takeover of Mandalore|Death Watch coup]].<ref name="The Star Wars Book" />

==History==
{{Quote|House Vizsla?"<br>"She's Death Watch."<br>"Traitor!|Two members of the [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protectors]], regarding [[Sabine Wren]]|<ref name="The Protector of Concord Dawn" />}}
[[File:House_Vizsla_Death_Watch.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Mandalorians bowing to a member of House Vizsla]]
The House was founded by Tarre Vizsla, the first Mandalorian [[Jedi]] and creator of the Darksaber.<ref name="Return of the Mandalorian" /> At some point later, the Darksaber was kept in the [[Imperial Palace|Jedi Temple]]. During the [[fall of the Old Republic]], members of House Vizsla stole<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" /> Tarre Vizsla's Darksaber from the temple. With the Darksaber as a symbol of power, House Vizsla managed to conquer and unify all of [[Mandalore]] for a period of time.<ref name="Trials of the Darksaber" />

[[File:PreVizsla-MF68.png|thumb|right|250px|Mand'alor Pre Vizsla of the eponymous Mandalorian clan and house led the Death Watch.]]
Following the [[Great Clan Wars|Mandalorian Civil War]], the head of House and Clan Vizsla, [[Pre Vizsla]] became the [[Governor]] of [[Concordia]]. While publicly supporting the [[New Mandalorians]]' pacifist government under [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]], Vizsla secretly led Death Watch in a secret alliance with [[Count]] [[Dooku]]'s [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="The Mandalore Plot" />

During the [[Imperial Era|reign]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], House Vizsla sided with the Empire in hopes of gaining more power under the leadership of Mandalore’s Imperial Governor [[Gar Saxon]]<ref name="Rebels Recon">{{RebelsRecon|Gg6vtqWPh3c|#3.06: Inside "Imperial Super Commandos" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-imperial-super-commandos}}</ref> of Clan Saxon.<ref name="Zero Hour" /> Due to their affiliations with Death Watch, House Vizsla and the clans which belonged to it, such as Clan Wren, were considered sworn enemies of the Mandalorian Protectors,<ref name="The Protector of Concord Dawn" /> elite warriors from their culture<ref name="The Protectors">{{Databank|the-protectors|The Protectors}}</ref> who were once bodyguards for the late Duchess Satine.<ref name="Inside Twin Suns">{{RebelsRecon|8eIZsJsck7A|#3.20: Inside "Twin Suns" &#124; Star Wars Rebels|sw_url=video/rebels-recon-inside-twin-suns}}</ref> Since the violent end of her reign, the Protectors had relocated to Concord Dawn, but their leader [[Fenn Rau]] and other members of his organization treated House Vizsla as synonymous with Death Watch and declared such Mandalorians to be traitors.<ref name="The Protector of Concord Dawn" /> House Vizsla would see [[Mandalorian Civil War (Imperial Era)|internal conflict]] following a [[skirmish on Krownest]], between Clans Saxon and Wren, with Clan Saxon having Imperial support.<ref name="Zero Hour" /> 

During the [[New Republic Era]], [[Paz Vizsla]] was part of [[the Tribe]],<ref name="The Sin">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref> a group of the [[Children of the Watch]], who were a religious Mandalorian sect that followed the [[Mandalorian Creed]] and the [[Way of the Mandalore]].<ref name="Heiress">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> The group lived in a [[Nevarro Mandalorian covert|Mandalorian covert]] on [[Nevarro]]. Following [[Din Djarin]]'s [[Clash on Nevarro|mission]] to rescue [[Din Grogu|Grogu]], a [[Force-sensitive]] child, Paz Vizsla and the rest of the tribe were drawn into public action.<ref name="The Sin" /> Their reveal resulted in the covert's destruction by an [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] led by [[Moff]] [[Gideon]].<ref name="Redemption">{{TheMandalorian|Redemption}}</ref> Paz and "[[The Armorer]]" were the only two survivors alongside Din Djarin. Following Djarin's [[Hunt for Grogu|quest]]<ref name="Return of the Mandalorian" /> to bring Grogu to the Jedi,<ref name="The Rescue">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 16: The Rescue}}</ref> Djarin, Paz, and the Armorer reconnected on the [[space station]] [[Glavis Ringworld]], where they began another [[Mandalorian covert|covert]]. After learning that Djarin had acquired the Darksaber through combat, Paz Vizsla challenged him to a [[Fight for the Darksaber|duel]] to regain his clan's sword, but failed.<ref name="Return of the Mandalorian" />

